---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const repo = ''; // TODO: add your public GitHub repo URL; the link appears automatically
---

<Layout title="Projects" description="Projects by Racell Sincioco, with architecture and engineering notes.">
	<section id="projects">
		<h1>Projects</h1>

		<article class="project">
			<h2>Serverless cloud portfolio</h2>
			<p>
				A portfolio built like a production deployment rather than a template. The frontend is a
				static Astro site on Firebase Hosting. A containerized Node.js API on Cloud Run counts
				visits in Firestore, and everything is provisioned with Terraform.
			</p>

			<dl class="facts">
				<dt>Stack</dt>
				<dd>Astro, Firebase Hosting, Cloud Run, Firestore, Terraform, GitHub Actions, BigQuery</dd>

				<dt>Delivery</dt>
				<dd>
					GitHub Actions authenticates with Workload Identity Federation, so no static service
					account keys exist anywhere. Gitleaks blocks commits that contain secrets.
				</dd>

				<dt>Analytics</dt>
				<dd>
					No tracking scripts or cookies. Firebase Hosting access logs are routed to BigQuery and
					queried with standard SQL.
				</dd>

				<dt>Decisions</dt>
				<dd>Each major choice is recorded as an Architecture Decision Record in the repository.</dd>
			</dl>

			{
				repo && (
					<p>
						<a href={repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
							View the source on GitHub
						</a>
					</p>
				)
			}
		</article>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.project h2 {
		font-size: 1.6rem;
	}

	.facts {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 9rem 1fr;
		gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
		margin: 2rem 0 1.5rem;
		padding-top: 1.5rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	dt {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--ink-soft);
	}

	dd {
		margin: 0;
	}

	@media (max-width: 560px) {
		.facts {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 0.1rem;
		}

		dd {
			margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
		}
	}
</style>